[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346561988,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346652105,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346658243,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346661674,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346664675,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.3466674,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346670163,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346672726,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346676474,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346708976,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346714076,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346719009,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer: noise simulations under a retained calibration export, design power analyses, parameter sweeps | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346725114,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346729263,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (v5e-8 shape) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend, so no repository simulation uses it | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346733459,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346737954,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346742528,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.34674693,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346751409,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346755109,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.34675897,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346762605,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346766929,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346770557,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346774096,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346777868,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346781838,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346787708,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346791921,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346797975,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346814554,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346820231,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346824517,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346828654,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346832613,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346836603,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346840385,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346844298,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346847897,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346851728,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346855414,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346859436,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346863168,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346867207,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346871419,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346875731,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346887229000004,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346905656,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346911231,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.34691615,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346920839,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.34692556,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346929293,"data":"- A kernel is private, has GPU and internet enabled, and holds no IBM\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346933229,"data":"  credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.3469372,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346941157,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE` and selects the GPU through it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346945472,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346949334,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346953361,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.3469574,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape are in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346961648,"data":"  `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":60.346965526,"data":"\n"}
